## Context

The code+data reproducibility archive was deposited on Zenodo 2026-06-16
(ticket 0676): **concept DOI 10.5281/zenodo.20715179** (all versions, always
resolves to the latest snapshot). The current manuscript's "Data & Code
Availability" still points only to the mutable GitHub URL — added by closed
ticket 0509, before the deposit existed. GitHub is not a persistent
identifier; the mission requires locatable, citable data.

Blocked-by 0665 deliberately: the citation upgrade belongs to the
preprint/v2 manuscript pass that accompanies the arXiv push, NOT to 0665
itself (0665 posts the tag PDF byte-identical). When 0665 closes this becomes
ready and the reminder fires. See the publication-strategy Imagine [[0675]].

## What to do (in the preprint/v2 manuscript pass)

1. In `slides/manuscript/main.tex` "Data & Code Availability", cite the Zenodo
   **concept** DOI (10.5281/zenodo.20715179) — not the version DOI — so the
   line stays correct across future snapshots. Keep the GitHub URL as the
   human-browsable source if desired, but the citable identifier is the DOI.
2. Cut a fresh Zenodo **version** for the v2 snapshot (Zenodo "New version" on
   record 20715180) at the preprint tag, under the same concept DOI.
3. Set `CITATION.cff` `preferred-citation.doi` to the assigned arXiv id
   (replacing the `10.XXXXX/arXiv.XXXXX` placeholder) once 0665 mints it.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Manuscript "Data & Code Availability" cites the Zenodo concept DOI
- [ ] CITATION.cff preferred-citation DOI = the arXiv id (no placeholder)
- [ ] A v2 Zenodo version exists for the preprint snapshot (same concept DOI)
